bly\" in Q3. Its 2027 capex is up only 12%, so it looks fundable through debt.\n- Pellham's 2027 capex is up 18%. Debt alone evidently isn't enough for it, because it is cutting back.\n\n**Equity**\n- Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering after investor demand fell short.\n- Two other utility share offerings were cut back in size.\n- The window looks open only for smaller deals, not large follow-ons.\n\n**Effect on spending**\n- Pellham is the largest grid-equipment buyer. It plans to cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes until financing improves.\n- That is negative for grid-equipment orders. It matters for VLTX because utilities account for 62% of its orders.\n\n**Gaps**\n- The sources are thin: three short documents.\n- They had no data on issuance volumes, debt capacity, ratings headroom, equity valuations, at-the-market (ATM) share programmes, or dollar equity needs. I haven't inferred any of these.\n\nDetails are in n5.r1 (debt) and n6.r1 (equity).","ttft_ms":1959,"type":"result","duration_ms":29884,"uuid":"79eb17ca-9fd8-44fc-ae9b-ce2856d29943","ttft_stream_ms":1360,"time_to_request_ms":553,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":14,"system_prompt":40,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":96,"input_hooks":24,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":164,"tool_pool_refresh":4,"init_message":57,"init_frame_send":24,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":12,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":14,"autocompact":23,"request_announcements":34,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":15,"message_normalization":6,"client_creation":9,"request_build":10},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":180,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":99,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":173,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":98,"process_rss_mib_result":189,"process_anon_mib_result":108,"process_peak_rss_mib":190,"process_cpu_ms_turn":595,"process_wall_ms_turn":29